All three strategies were launched within 48 hours (January 6-7, 2025) as parallel responses to the AutomateFlow disruption, each championed by a different team lead pursuing their area of expertise. This fragmented approach ultimately created integration failures and technical debt, leading to a unified strategy consolidation later in January.

